{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Forty-two cities.</b> Corresponding to the forty-two stations at which Israel encamped — and in all of them they were sojourners — so they gave to the Levites, who had no portion in the land, forty-two cities. And the cities of refuge were to be from among the cities of the Levites, because one who flees to his city of refuge is a sojourner there, and there is reason to fear lest the inhabitants of the land say to him: 'You are a sojourner in the land.' Therefore He commanded that the cities of refuge be from among the cities of the Levites, for the Levites too are sojourners and will say to him — 'the blemish in yourself, do not mention to your fellow' — along the lines of what is said (Exodus 23:9): ״וְאַתֶּם יְדַעְתֶּם אֶת נֶפֶשׁ הַגֵּר כִּי גֵרִים הֱיִיתֶם״, and in the manner of what is said (Genesis 15:13): ״כִּי גֵר יִהְיֶה זַרְעֲךָ בְּאֶרֶץ לֹא לָהֶם״ — that is, in a land that does not belong to them, namely the land of the inhabitants of the earth; for Joseph relocated them to cities so that they would be sojourners there, in order that they would not be able to say to Israel: 'You are sojourners.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:02.338972906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}